cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TAKTO ONE: a sensor-integrated, tendon-driven hand exoskeleton"
message: "If you use this project, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sebastian
    family-names: Molano
    affiliation: Hochschule Anhalt
repository-code: "https://github.com/molanocortes/takto-one"
abstract: >-
  TAKTO ONE is an open hardware and software platform for a tendon-driven wearable
  hand exoskeleton. It integrates twelve AS5600 magnetic joint encoders, a Teensy 4.1
  controller that owns a Dynamixel motor bus through a 74HC241 half-duplex interface,
  two custom PCBs, and a browser-based operator console with a live 3D digital twin.
keywords:
  - robotics
  - exoskeleton
  - wearable robotics
  - hand rehabilitation
  - tendon-driven
  - open hardware
  - embedded systems
license: Apache-2.0
year: 2026
